WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.160
Speaker 1: OK, so I want to lay this out now
just to get it on the record relatively early.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.890
Normally, I don't comment about an election
that's not the immediate next election.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:14.150
So in 2017, people would call in and they'd
say, hey, what do you think about 2020?

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.330
This, that?

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.250
And I'd say, we have to focus on twenty eighteen.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.930
That's the immediate question right now.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.360
What happens in twenty eighteen.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.320
But I actually do want to talk about twenty
twenty four today a little bit because I worry

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.960
that there's lots of people just missing what's
taking place and not seeing what is increasingly

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.310
a very disturbing situation.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.710
The bottom line is this.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.220
I believe that if there's a so-called rematch
in twenty four between Trump and Biden, that

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.760
that's very, very bad for Joe Biden.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.489
I don't think that looks good.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:47.070
And if Joe Biden chooses not to run for reelection
and it is Kamala Harris instead, who is the

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.680
Democratic presidential nominee, I think that
that also doesn't look very good.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.629
And I'm going to lay out why now.

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:56.710
I'm going to mention Joe Biden's age here.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:01.239
Joe Biden would be 82 at the time of the twenty
twenty four election.

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:03.910
Donald Trump would also be 78 at that time.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.560
And one might argue there's really not that
much difference.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.500
It's just two old white guys.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.000
But the difference is that Donald Trump has
a cult of followers, a cult of personality

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.260
around him that afflicts his supporters for
whom Trump's age is not going to be a factor.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.970
While I believe that because of the nature
of Joe Biden's support and because of the

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:27.540
nature, particularly of the progressive wing
of the Democratic Party and the preferences

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:34.810
of Democratic voters, the idea of voting for
and 82 year old in 2024 is going to impact

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:38.540
those more predisposed to vote for Joe Biden.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:44.100
Then it will affect those likely or considering
voting for Donald Trump in twenty, twenty

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.100
four.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.650
So in other words, what I'm saying is Biden's
age will work against him more than Trump's

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.610
age will work against Trump.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.730
So let's now get into my thought process.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:02:00.010
First and foremost, I'm getting the sense
just at a basic level, that in general, a

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:03.480
so-called rematch is going to be very tough
for Joe Biden.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:09.740
And in addition to the concept of a rematch
or one of our Redit viewers put a post up

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:14.830
on our Redit that calls it like a sort of
final showdown, I think that it will invigorate

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:17.890
the right far more than it will invigorate
the left.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:21.770
That's one scenario, the final showdown rematch
between Trump and Biden.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:23.500
I don't think it's very good for Joe Biden.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:28.060
Now, there's a different scenario that's possible,
which is that Joe Biden, as some suspect,

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:34.640
might not run for a second term in 2024 and
then Kamala Harris will either be handed or

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.230
might have to fight for the Democratic nomination.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:42.320
There's still a long time until 2024, but
all of those scenarios, I think, are also

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.760
problematic.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:49.180
Kamala Harris has maintained a relatively
low profile so far, and she has low approval

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.180
ratings.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:54.470
That doesn't give me much confidence about
Harris vs. Trump in twenty twenty four.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:59.000
If you look at the latest real Clear Politics
average of approval polls, Kamala Harris is

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.430
now underwater.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:04.640
Her negatives, her disapproval is higher than
her approval.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.700
For better or worse, she's taken some real
hits when it comes to her handling of the

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.700
border.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.950
Now, you might say what handling?

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:15.710
Rightly or wrongly, Joe Biden tasked her with
the border problem.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.390
Her approval on that is very low now.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:18.390
It's early.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:19.990
Things could change between now and twenty,
twenty four.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:26.000
But as of right now, I am not at all confident
that if Kamala Harris is just handed the Democratic

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.930
nomination, meaning Biden says, I'm not running,
but Kamala Harris is running and no serious

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:35.420
Democratic primary takes place and she's the
nominee.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.460
I don't think Harris does well against Donald
Trump in twenty twenty four.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.810
In fact, I find it really difficult to see
a scenario where she wins.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:48.500
Now, the other scenario would be Joe Biden
says he's not running and Harris does run.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:54.500
But there's a big primary fight, which Kamala
Harris ultimately wins because of her low

00:03:54.500 --> 00:04:01.810
approval if Kamala Harris has to fight her
way through an ugly primary to get that nomination.

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:05.890
It also strikes me as a recipe for disaster
similar to 2016.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:10.560
The third scenario would be Biden doesn't
run.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:17.570
Comilla fights for the nomination, but she
loses and someone else is the Democratic nominee.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.970
That I do think is too early to talk about.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:23.080
And we just have no idea who that might be.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.690
We have no idea how they might match up against
Donald.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:27.100
It's just too hypothetical.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:32.360
But the two scenarios I'm focused on, which
are the problematic ones, which are Biden

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:37.610
does run for reelection or Biden doesn't and
Carmela's the nominee, whether she just gets

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:43.290
it handed to her or she fights for it and
wins it, if you give me an even money bet

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.290
today.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:49.280
I'm probably betting on Trump in those scenarios
based on what I currently see as the energy

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:55.780
of the Democratic Party and the energy of
the Republican Party, part of it is that even

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.210
in 20, 20, right.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:01.240
There's this urgent emergency of removing
Donald Trump.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:06.260
The the the energy and enthusiasm around Biden
was relatively muted.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:11.630
Now, Biden, fortunately won by many millions
of votes nationally, but it was small differences

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:12.949
in just a few states.

00:05:12.949 --> 00:05:15.110
If they had gone the other way, Trump would
have won.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:17.740
It's similar to Trump winning in 16.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:22.820
If just a few states went slightly differently,
Hillary Clinton would have been the winner

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:23.820
in 2016.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:29.210
So that also makes me concerned with Trump
four years in the rearview mirror that there

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:33.850
will be, again, Democrats who, after eight
years of Obama said, I'm not out for whatever

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:34.850
reason.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.660
I'm not going to go out and vote in this Hillary
versus Trump thing.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:37.680
And then Trump won.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.350
A repeat of that also scares me.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:44.460
And then in addition to that, as we see at
these Trump rallies, the cult of personality

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.440
around Donald Trump, the fact that the Republican
Party, whether they're pretending or whether

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.820
they seriously like Trump, it doesn't matter.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.100
They're basically behind him.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.040
They're not abandoning him.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.210
That is troubling.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:06:00.169
And there is really I mean, it really seems
like there's nothing Trump can do to lose

00:06:00.169 --> 00:06:02.480
the support that he has, or at least most
of it.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:08.350
So I think twenty, twenty four is real trouble
in a rematch against Joe Biden or against

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:09.550
Kamala Harris?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.490
I'm not saying I have a better idea.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:15.990
I think Trump will be very strong in twenty
four if he's the nominee.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:18.810
So if you have a different perspective, I
would love to hear from you.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.710
And I understand I'm breaking my own rule.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:26.030
I usually only talk about the next election,
but the circumstances are unique and the next

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.490
election is 20 two.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:33.669
But it relates so much to twenty four that
we really have sort of like a three year period

00:06:33.669 --> 00:06:36.310
that I see as a package in my mind.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:39.050
So send me your thoughts about this.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:44.120
And of course, if twenty, twenty two goes
disastrously for the Trump wing of the Republican

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.889
Party, that weakens Trump dramatically.

00:06:47.889 --> 00:06:51.370
But I don't know that that's actually going
to be the outcome.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:53.410
So let me know how worried you are about this.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:07:53.370
If you agree, disagree, find me on Twitter

00:07:53.370 --> 00:08:30.190
at David Pakman.

